% A literate source with code chunks in blocks, woven into the test-bilingual
% notes (test-bilingual-contents.tex inputs it).  noweave writes the chunk
% index after the file's last code chunk, so where that chunk stands decides
% whether both editions get the index: test-bilingual.sh counts its entries
% in each edition's .aux.

<<[[shared.py]]>>=
print("SHAREDCHUNK")
@

\begin{en} % sync en=d00efb sv=f05749
ENPROSE before a chunk of its own.

<<[[en.py]]>>=
print("ENCHUNK")
@
\end{en}
\begin{sv}
SVPROSE before a chunk of its own.

<<[[sv.py]]>>=
print("SVCHUNK")
@
\end{sv}

The file's last chunk stands outside the blocks, as the documentation says, so
that the chunk index, which noweave writes after it, is in both editions.

<<[[shared.py]]>>=
print("the end")
@
